{
 "what": "inkrs against two other public ink runners, each a whole command (process start to exit) on the same RTX 5090, inputs and model window: UFSM, a C/CUDA port of the readers, Hecate and v8-in with its own fp16 tensor-core convolutions compiled ahead to SASS, and ink-sdk's v8-in lane. speedup is the alternative's wall over inkrs's, above 1 when inkrs is faster. Warm runs share each runner's caches across arms; in the cold runs every inkrs arm starts with empty inkrs and CUDA driver caches, so it compiles its PTX and, for Hecate, times cuDNN's algorithms. Each run is 2 untimed warm-ups then 6 pairs in ABBA order (ink-sdk: three jobs of 2 pairs, no warm-ups); the A/A noise is a run of inkrs against itself on the same model. Parity scores each runner's map against the references the inkrs gates use (villa eager, hecate.py, the v8-in release maps), in 1/255 levels; UFSM writes no coverage mask, so its coverage is checked by value. UFSM implements only v8-in's release convention, so its A-hn map fails against the PHerc. 306B recipe's convention. UFSM has no licence: only these measurements are published, not its code or maps",
 "gpu": "RTX 5090, driver 595.99.02",
 "date": "2026-11-11/12",
 "build": "an earlier v0.2 build; carry gives its A/Bs, through one intermediate build, to this binary, on the reader-v2, Reader V3, Hecate, 3D U-Net and v8-in benches, none slower",
 "alternatives": {
  "ufsm": "UFSM ink-ext, built locally for sm_120; fp16 only",
  "ink-sdk": "ink-sdk's v8-in lane (MIT), with PyTorch 2.13 cu129"
 },
 "models": {
  "s42": "hybrid_3d2d-seed42 (ink_9um), one map (layers 25-41, forward) of S1, stride 64; inkrs batch 64, UFSM batch 64",
  "v3": "Reader V3, one map (layers 25-41, forward) of S1, stride 192; batch 8 on both",
  "hec-bf16": "Hecate 9.6 um, one map (forward) of the whole PHerc. 1447 segment at 9.6 um (28 x 2682 x 2916), stride 32; inkrs bf16 at batch 32 against UFSM's fp16 at batch 32",
  "hec-fp32": "the same Hecate map; inkrs fp32 (TF32 convolutions) at batch 8 against UFSM's fp16 at batch 32",
  "v8": "v8-in, one map (forward, release convention) of the 41 x 1260 x 4410 PHerc. 306B crop; batch 16 on both",
  "v8both": "v8-in, both directions of the same crop; inkrs batch 16 against ink-sdk's v8-in lane, which runs the model repository's predict.py at its fixed batch 8"
 },
